---
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import StatusDot from '../ui/StatusDot.astro';
---

<section class="pt-16 pb-20 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-28">
  <div class="wrap grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12 lg:items-center">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7 animate-fade-up">
      <p class="eyebrow flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
        <span>{site.role}</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>{site.location}</span>
        {site.availability && (
          <>
            <span class="flex basis-full items-center gap-2">
              <StatusDot />
              {site.availability}
            </span>
          </>
        )}
      </p>

      <h1 class="mt-6 text-display text-fg text-balance">
        Backends for multi-stage workflows where every decision is on the record.
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted text-pretty">
        I design and run Django and PostgreSQL systems on Google Cloud. My flagship is the
        backend for a scholarship programme: the full award lifecycle, 12 staff
        roles, multi-stage approvals and a change history on every record that matters.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-4">
        <a
          href="/projects/"
          class="btn btn-primary"
        >
          Read the case studies
        </a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="link text-sm font-medium">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="lg:col-span-5 animate-fade-up anim-delay-200">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 480 172"
        class="w-full max-w-md lg:max-w-none text-line-strong"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc"
        fill="none"
      >
        <title id="arch-title">Anatomy of a safe write request</title>
        <desc id="arch-desc">
          A client sends a request with an idempotency key. The API authenticates and validates it, then writes
          the state change and an outbox event to PostgreSQL in one transaction. Workers read the outbox and
          send side effects such as emails and webhooks with retries; deliveries that keep failing go to a
          dead-letter queue for alerting and replay.
        </desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="arch-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M0 0.5 L7 4 L0 7.5" fill="none" stroke="var(--subtle)" stroke-width="1.2" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Edges -->
        <g stroke="var(--subtle)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)">
          <path d="M134 44 H173" />
          <path d="M305 44 H344" />
          <path d="M411 68 V118" />
          <path d="M346 144 H307" />
          <path d="M175 144 H136" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
        </g>

        <!-- Edge labels -->
        <g class="font-mono fill-subtle" font-size="10.5">
          <text x="154" y="36" text-anchor="middle">POST</text>
          <text x="325" y="36" text-anchor="middle">1 txn</text>
          <text x="419" y="97">outbox</text>
          <text x="326" y="136" text-anchor="middle">send</text>
          <text x="155" y="136" text-anchor="middle">fail</text>
        </g>

        <!-- Nodes -->
        <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" class="fill-surface">
          <rect x="4.5" y="20.5" width="129" height="47" rx="6" />
          <rect x="175.5" y="20.5" width="129" height="47" rx="6" />
          <rect x="346.5" y="20.5" width="129" height="47" rx="6" />
          <rect x="346.5" y="120.5" width="129" height="47" rx="6" />
          <rect x="175.5" y="120.5" width="129" height="47" rx="6" />
          <rect x="4.5" y="120.5" width="129" height="47" rx="6" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
        </g>

        <g class="font-mono">
          <g font-size="12.5" class="fill-fg" font-weight="500">
            <text x="18" y="41">client</text>
            <text x="189" y="41">api</text>
            <text x="372" y="41">postgres</text>
            <text x="360" y="141">workers</text>
            <text x="189" y="141">side effects</text>
            <text x="18" y="141">dead letter</text>
          </g>
          <g font-size="10.5" class="fill-muted">
            <text x="18" y="57">Idempotency-Key</text>
            <text x="189" y="57">auth · validate</text>
            <text x="360" y="57">state + outbox</text>
            <text x="360" y="157">retry · backoff</text>
            <text x="189" y="157">email · webhooks</text>
            <text x="18" y="157">alert · replay</text>
          </g>
          <circle cx="363" cy="37" r="3" class="fill-accent" />
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-subtle">
        fig. 1 — one write, end to end. The idempotency key makes retries safe, the state
        change and its outbox event commit together, and workers deliver side effects
        with retries.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
